================================================================================
  STUDENT LOAN TRACKER — PROJECT GUIDE (READ_ME)
================================================================================

This document maps the solution so you can find the right file when you want to
change behavior, layout, data, or startup. It focuses on source and project
files (not build output like bin/ or obj/, and not IDE folders like .vs/).

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT THIS APP IS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  • Desktop app built with Avalonia UI (.NET 8), MVVM pattern.
  • Loans are stored in a local SQLite file (see DatabaseInitializer).
  • Payment schedules and charts use amortization math in LoanCalculator.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SOLUTION LAYOUT (THREE PROJECTS)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  StudentLoanTracker.Core
    Domain types, validation, and calculator. No UI, no database code.

  StudentLoanTracker.Data
    SQLite access implementing the Core repository interface.

  StudentLoanTracker.App
    Avalonia UI (XAML views), view models, navigation, dependency injection,
    and the executable entry point.

  StudentLoanTracker.sln
    Visual Studio / dotnet solution that references the three projects above.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
QUICK “WHERE DO I LOOK?”
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  Change window title, header text, default size
    → StudentLoanTracker.App\Views\MainWindow.axaml

  Change loan list screen (buttons, grid columns, empty state)
    → Views\LoanListView.axaml
    → ViewModels\LoanListViewModel.cs (commands, loading, HasLoans, etc.)

  Change add/edit loan form (labels, fields, layout)
    → Views\LoanDetailView.axaml
    → ViewModels\LoanDetailViewModel.cs (save/cancel, binding properties)

  Change payment schedule table or “extra payment” behavior on that screen
    → Views\ScheduleView.axaml
    → ViewModels\ScheduleViewModel.cs
    → Core\LoanCalculator.cs (actual month-by-month math)

  Change charts (labels, layout) or how series are built
    → Views\ChartsView.axaml
    → ViewModels\ChartsViewModel.cs
    → Core\LoanCalculator.cs (same schedule data as the grid)

  Change validation rules (allowed rates, term limits, etc.)
    → Core\LoanValidator.cs

  Change how loans are stored or add columns / migrations
    → Data\DatabaseInitializer.cs (schema)
    → Data\SqliteLoanRepository.cs (SQL + mapping)
    → Core\Loan.cs (properties must match what you persist)

  Change how screens switch without opening the window type
    → ViewModels\MainWindowViewModel.cs (implements INavigationService)
    → Services\INavigationService.cs (interface)

  Register services or set database path at startup
    → App.axaml.cs

  Change fonts / global theme / ViewLocator registration
    → App.axaml

  Change how a ViewModel type finds its View (.axaml)
    → ViewLocator.cs

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FILE-BY-FILE REFERENCE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

ROOT
----
  StudentLoanTracker.sln
    Solution file: lists projects and build configurations.

  READ_ME.txt
    This guide.

  .gitignore / .gitattributes (if present)
    Git ignore rules and line-ending settings; not part of runtime behavior.


STUDENTLOANTRACKER.CORE  (class library — business rules & types)
-----------------------------------------------------------------
  StudentLoanTracker.Core.csproj
    Project file: targets .NET 8, enables nullable reference types.

  Loan.cs
    Data model for one loan (name, servicer, principal, rate, term, dates,
    notes, etc.). Shared by UI, calculator, and SQLite layer.

  PaymentScheduleEntry.cs
    One row of an amortization schedule (payment #, date, amounts, balance).

  LoanValidator.cs
    Static validation: principal, interest rate range, term range, minimum
    payment. Used before save and before the calculator builds a schedule.

  LoanCalculator.cs
    Amortization engine: builds payment schedule, payoff month count, total
    interest. Uses standard level-payment (PMT-style) logic plus optional
    extra monthly payment.

  ILoanCalculator.cs
    Interface implemented by LoanCalculator so the app can inject a fake or
    alternate implementation in tests.

  ILoanRepository.cs
    Interface for loading/saving/deleting loans (implemented in Data project).


STUDENTLOANTRACKER.DATA  (class library — SQLite)
-------------------------------------------------
  StudentLoanTracker.Data.csproj
    Project file: references Core and Microsoft.Data.Sqlite.

  DatabaseInitializer.cs
    Creates the app data folder under the user’s ApplicationData and ensures
    the Loans table exists. Defines the CREATE TABLE statement.

  SqliteLoanRepository.cs
    Implements ILoanRepository: SELECT/INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE against SQLite,
    maps rows to Loan objects (Guid and DateTime as strings in the DB).


STUDENTLOANTRACKER.APP  (executable Avalonia application)
---------------------------------------------------------
  StudentLoanTracker.App.csproj
    Project file: Avalonia packages, LiveCharts, CommunityToolkit.Mvvm, DI,
    references to Core and Data.

  app.manifest
    Windows application manifest (compatibility / DPI-related defaults for
    desktop). Usually leave as-is unless you have a specific Windows need.

  Program.cs
    Main entry: builds the Avalonia app and starts the classic desktop
    lifetime (normal windowed app).

  App.axaml
    Application-level XAML: Fluent theme, DataGrid theme include, and the
    ViewLocator in DataTemplates so ContentControl can resolve views.

  App.axaml.cs
    On startup: optional validation plugin removal, SQLite initialization,
    Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection setup (repository, calculator,
    MainWindowViewModel), assigns DataContext to MainWindow.

  ViewLocator.cs
    IDataTemplate: given a ViewModelBase, loads the matching *View* class
    by replacing “ViewModel” with “View” in the type name.

  Services\INavigationService.cs
    Interface for NavigateTo(viewModel) and NavigateToLoanList() used by
    child view models to change the current screen.


  ViewModels\ViewModelBase.cs
    Empty base class inheriting ObservableObject; ViewLocator only matches
    types derived from this.

  ViewModels\MainWindowViewModel.cs
    Holds CurrentViewModel (the active screen). Implements INavigationService.
    Creates or reuses LoanListViewModel when returning to the list.

  ViewModels\LoanListViewModel.cs
    ObservableCollection of loans, selected row, status message, HasLoans /
    ShowEmptyState for UI. Commands: add, edit, delete, refresh, schedule,
    charts. Loads data via ILoanRepository.

  ViewModels\LoanDetailViewModel.cs
    Two-way fields for one Loan; Save copies to entity, validates, Add or
    Update repository, then navigates to list. Cancel navigates back without
    saving. Title reflects add vs edit.

  ViewModels\ScheduleViewModel.cs
    Wraps one loan + ILoanCalculator; ExtraMonthlyPayment triggers schedule
    refresh; exposes totals and payoff date for the schedule view.

  ViewModels\ChartsViewModel.cs
    Same loan + calculator + extra payment; builds LiveCharts series for
    balance line and principal vs interest pie.


  Views\MainWindow.axaml
    Root window: title bar text, size, header strip, ContentControl bound
    to CurrentViewModel.

  Views\MainWindow.axaml.cs
    Code-behind for the window (typically InitializeComponent only).

  Views\LoanListView.axaml
    Loan list UI: toolbar, DataGrid, empty-state panel, status line.

  Views\LoanListView.axaml.cs
    Code-behind for the user control (usually minimal).

  Views\LoanDetailView.axaml
    Add/edit loan form: text boxes, numeric inputs, date picker, notes,
    validation display, save/cancel.

  Views\LoanDetailView.axaml.cs
    Code-behind for the user control (usually minimal).

  Views\ScheduleView.axaml
    Back button, loan name, extra payment controls, summary numbers,
    read-only schedule DataGrid.

  Views\ScheduleView.axaml.cs
    Code-behind for the user control (usually minimal).

  Views\ChartsView.axaml
    Back button, loan name, extra payment, totals, CartesianChart and
    PieChart bound to view model series.

  Views\ChartsView.axaml.cs
    Code-behind for the user control (usually minimal).


GENERATED / BUILD ARTIFACTS (DO NOT EDIT BY HAND)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  **/obj/** and **/bin/**
    Compiler output, including CommunityToolkit.Mvvm generated *.g.cs files
    that implement [ObservableProperty] and [RelayCommand] for your view models.

  Editing those generated files would be overwritten on the next build.


VIEWMODELS AND AUTO-GENERATED CODE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  ViewModels use CommunityToolkit.Mvvm attributes. At compile time, the toolkit
  generates partial class members (properties, commands). You edit the partial
  class file in ViewModels\; the generator fills in the repetitive INotifyPropertyChanged
  and ICommand wiring.

================================================================================
